 <div class="carousel-slide active" data-slide="0">
 <div class="contaminant-grid">
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="chlorine"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.9%</span><h2>Chlorine</h2>
 <p>Chlorine reacts with organic matter in water, forming disinfection byproducts (DBPs) linked to health risks like cancer, birth defects, and respiratory issues. </p></div></div>
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="bacteria"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.9%</span><h2>Bacteria</h2><p>Bacteria in drinking water can lead to illnesses like gastrointestinal issues, and serious infections such as skin and urinary tract infections.</p></div></div>
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="pfas"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.66%</span><h2>PFAS</h2><p>PFAS in drinking water is linked to hormonal disruptions, weakened immune systems, increased infection susceptibility, and liver damage.
</p></div></div>
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="viruses"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.9%</span><h2>Viruses</h2><p> Viruses in drinking water can lead to hepatitis, vomiting, diarrhea, and fever, particularly affecting vulnerable groups like children and the elderly.</p></div></div>
 </div>
 </div>

 
 <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide="1">
 <div class="contaminant-grid">
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="microplastics"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.9%</span><h2>Microplastics</h2><p>Microplastics can pose potential health risks, including endocrine disruption and cellular damage. They are also linked to potential health concerns such as hormone disruption, and long-term organ damage.
</p></div></div>
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="pharmaceuticals"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.9%</span><h2>Pharmaceuticals</h2><p>Pharmaceuticals in water can disrupt hormones, affect organ function, and lead to antibiotic resistance, posing significant health risks over time.
.</p></div></div>
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="pesticides"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.99%</span><h2>Pesticides</h2><p> Pesticides in water, often from agricultural runoff, can lead to serious health concerns, including hormonal disruptions, nervous system damage, and an increased risk of cancer.
</p></div></div>
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="bad-taste"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.9%</span><h2>Bad Taste</h2><p> Unpleasant taste and smell in water are often caused by chlorine, sulfur, and organic compounds. These impurities not only affect the flavor but can also indicate the presence of harmful substances.
</p></div></div>
 </div>
 </div>

 
 <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide="2">
 <div class="contaminant-grid">
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="pharmaceuticals"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.9%</span><h2>Fluoride </h2><p>Excessive fluoride in water can lead to health issues like fluorosis. Our advanced filtration system removes over 95% of fluoride, ensuring your water is safe, balanced, and free from harmful excesses.
</p></div></div>
 <div class="contaminant-card" id="pesticides"><div class="card-content"><span class="percentage">99.99%</span><h2>Heavy Metals</h2><p>Heavy metals in drinking water can lead to neurological damage, kidney and liver issues, and an increased risk of cancers like bladder and lung cancer.
